title: Office Document Spawning PowerShell Loader (Silent Lynx Espionage)
id: 4f406e72-b04b-4237-a9a9-b2a5e24652a5
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects macro-enabled Office documents spawning PowerShell in the
    Kazakhstan-nexus Silent Lynx (UAT-6275 / TAG-193) espionage campaign
    targeting government organizations across Central Asia and the CIS.
    The group's infection chains use macro-enabled documents and PS2EXE
    downloaders that fetch GitHub-hosted PowerShell and deliver custom
    reverse shells for interactive remote access.
references:
    - https://blog.talosintelligence.com/break-the-silence-kazakhstan-nexus-uat-6275-targets-cis-government-organizations/
    - https://www.recordedfuture.com/blog/tag193-regional-espionage-operations
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-10-15
tags:
    - attack.t1566
    - attack.t1204
    - attack.t1059
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_parent:
        ParentImage|endswith:
            - '\WINWORD.EXE'
            - '\EXCEL.EXE'
            - '\POWERPNT.EXE'
    selection_child:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\powershell.exe'
            - '\pwsh.exe'
            - '\cmd.exe'
    selection_suspicious:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'ps2exe'
            - 'Invoke-WebRequest'
            - 'DownloadString'
            - 'FromBase64String'
            - '-EncodedCommand'
    condition: selection_parent and selection_child and selection_suspicious
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate macro-driven automation or document workflows that invoke PowerShell
    - Signed enterprise macros that download or decode content on open
level: high
